angle:
Visual output first, safe by construction. Base: Design 3 (the owner's current priority is how the data looks). Grafts from the other two:

From Design 1:
- a verified-evidence list checked by sha256, plus an OpenGate brand type;
- copy entries that record their basis, and word-for-word notebook checks;
- a forged v2 test file that must keep every gate closed;
- devHook.ts as the only guarded import of dev code;
- a scan of the built files.

From Design 2:
- frozen shared code is never touched: app/src/analysis/**, app/src/types.ts, tools/**;
- the Upload listening evidence is an exact-RMS construction test on the real pipeline;
- no invented in-between frames.

Corrections to all three designs:
- 'Keeps X%' follows Exp 011 C25: ev[A] is computed from the payload's pcaExplainedVarianceRatio with Exp 011's own addition and rounding rules. It shows only while Exp 008's viewPreservation values for that view are shown (G2a.4). It is never shown for a payload without accepted evidence, such as an Upload.
- The Exp 008 block key is viewPreservation, with a swappable parser.
- The Exp 012 caveat is the C05 template, with V filled from the accepted build record.
- Lines follow C23: E3 lines only in the XYZ view, worded 'closest in this 3D projection'; any other space stays hidden until an owner-approved wording exists.
- Evidence statuses follow C24: only 'decided' opens a gate.

What ships to visitors now (all evidence-independent):
- the canonical v0.7 Matte cloud with up to 40 crisp peak-frequency numbers that never overlap;
- a colour key that matches the drawn dots;
- the whole cloud shown at rest;
- X/Y/Z chips for exact 1D/2D/3D views with one scale;
- real-angle camera transitions;
- hover values, two-dot compare with values side by side;
- a transport with a full-clip waveform and a red playhead;
- Upload into the same scene, and the exports.

Gated features are absent for visitors. In dev builds the owner can preview them, marked UNVERIFIED, including compare audio with a detailed waveform and a red playhead. The Exp 011 description text comes last.

features.design:
- useUploadRun:
  - decodes with decodeToAnalysisRate (unchanged);
  - keeps `pcm = decoded.samples`;
  - posts `const copy = pcm.slice()` with [copy.buffer], replacing the transfer of the original;
  - drops stale runIds;
  - normalizes the result and stores the PCM under up:<runId>.
- The 'This file' panel shows only definition facts:
  - dots kept of windows;
  - duration and dot spacing (samplingHopSeconds);
  - analysis rate, FFT size and step;
  - source rate and channels, or 'not read from the header';
  - analysed range and band-limit note;
  - compute time;
  - 'decoded and resampled by this browser, not ffmpeg';
  - the downmix warning;
  - Download analysis (JSON).

- Evidence table: accepted records and payload statuses.
- Every gated feature with its state and plain reasons.
- The preview switch, and simulated evidence.
- Diagnostics:
  - decode origin, rate and duration difference;
  - Upload self-check '{k} of {n} dots match exactly';
  - dropped edges, and a centroidMaxHz mismatch;
  - visible-label count and overlap count (must be 0);
  - key-versus-pixel readback.

